<%# The contact form. partials/article/_body.html.erb adds it to the contact page. It is a plain
    ERB partial, and not raw HTML in the body of the `contact` page in Contentful. markdown_to_html
    runs SmartyPants, which makes each straight quotation mark in a raw HTML *attribute* curly.
    That breaks the field names of the form and its Stimulus attributes. The intro text above the
    form stays in Contentful, where a person can edit it.

    Keep the field names (name, email, message, and the honeypot `comment`) the same as in the
    Api::ContactController of the api. This form also works with no JavaScript: the method and the
    action do a native POST, then a 303 to /contact/success. With JavaScript, the `contact`
    Stimulus controller takes the submit, does a fetch, and shows a toast. %>
<form method="POST" action="/api/contact" class="form"
      data-controller="contact" data-action="submit->contact#submit" data-turbo="false"
      data-contact-site-key-value="<%= turnstile_site_key %>">
  <wa-input label="Your name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <wa-input label="Your email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <label class="hp">Comment <textarea name="comment" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></textarea></label>
  <wa-textarea label="What's on your mind?" name="message" rows="6" resize="auto" with-count required></wa-textarea>
  <%# The `contact` controller renders Cloudflare Turnstile here, and that render works with
      Turbo. With no sitekey in the configuration, the div stays empty and the Turnstile check of
      the api permits the message. It protects the JavaScript path only, because the POST with no
      JavaScript cannot run the widget. %>
  <div class="contact__turnstile" data-contact-target="turnstile"></div>
  <wa-button type="submit" variant="brand" appearance="accent" data-contact-target="submit">
    Send Message
    <%= icon_svg("classic", "solid", "paper-plane")&.sub("<svg", '<svg slot="end"') %>
  </wa-button>
</form>
